{:event/seq 15, :event/type :note, :event/at "2026-07-21T00:59:40.526Z", :adr/id "adr-2607202800-task-graph-edn-schema-kotoba-langgraph-integration", :event/actor "Jun Kawasaki", :event/agent "claude-code", :event/summary "Phase3 dispatchを実サーバーに対しdry-run無しで検証、UI表示経路とdesign-quality登録ギャップを確認", :event/body "com-junkawasaki/root manifest/repos.edn edit 前提だが確認: nbb -cp src scripts/manimani-server.cljs(port 7777)を起動し、task_graph_dispatch.cljs を dry-run無しで実行 → POST /api/work が実際に成功しWorkItem(id=taskgraph:kotoba-github-linguist-recognition:G-grammar-repo, state=inbox, risk=read-only)を作成、task-graph-ledger.edn に :dispatched イベント(:event/seq 2)が実際に追記されたことを確認。再実行では dispatched-count=0 となり冪等性ガードが機能することも確認。バグ発見: scripts/repo-loop-scheduler.cljs と scripts/task_graph_dispatch.cljs の MANIMANI_LOCAL_URL 既定値は http://127.0.0.1:7778 だが、実際の manimani-server(src/manimani/server_host.cljs)の既定ポートは 7777 — 既存の repo-loop-scheduler.cljs から引き継いだ既定値の不一致(要修正、follow-up)。UI経路確認: orgs/gftdcojp/local-manimani の src/manimani/ui.cljc の work-tab は /api/work の結果を title/risk/state付きカードでレンダリングし、state別ボタン(inbox→Prepare、review→Human approve、approved→Execute)を提供 — dispatchしたWorkItemはこのUIにそのまま表示・操作可能であることをコード確認(ブラウザ実描画はChrome拡張未接続のため未確認)。design-quality gapを発見: local-manimani の ui.cljc は kotoba-ui.core(:as kui)を実際に使用しておりkotoba-uiの正当なconsumerだが、90-docs/design-quality/design-quality.datoms.edn の登録リブラリ一覧(appkit/kami-creative-studio/kami-studio/kotoba-ui/liquid-glass-ui/uikit)に local-manimani は含まれていない — orgs/kotoba-lang/design-quality(決定論的HIG/WCAGスコアラー、ADR-2607132300)での採点対象として登録漏れの可能性、follow-up候補。"}
{:event/seq 16, :event/type :note, :event/at "2026-07-21T01:30:22.791Z", :adr/id "adr-2607202800-task-graph-edn-schema-kotoba-langgraph-integration", :event/actor "Jun Kawasaki", :event/agent "claude-code", :event/summary "セッション終了サマリ: local-manimani を design-quality に登録・実修正で75.56→100.00/100達成、web/dist ビルド不能の回帰も発見・修正", :event/body "Phase 2/3実装後のフォローアップとして、local-manimani(kotoba-ui.core consumer)を90-docs/design-quality/design-quality.datoms.edn に新規登録し、kotoba-lang/design-quality の決定論的:auditレイヤーでスコアリング(初回75.56/100、findings: responsive/tap-targets/dynamic-viewport)。gftdcojp/local-manimani PR#60でこの3件を実修正: (1) .h-screenに100dvhフォールバック追加(Tailwindの@layer utilities内で自身のCSSを後置しcascadeで勝たせる方式、クラス名変更不要)、(2) .liquid-glass__button/.liquid-glass__icon-buttonにmin-height:44px + tailwind.config.jsのsafelist追加(これらのクラスは外部依存kotoba-ui.coreが実行時に出すもので、local-manimani自身のソースに文字列として現れないためTailwindのcontentベースpurgeが黙ってルールを削除していたことを発見、safelistで解決)、(3) @media(max-width:360px)でnav-bar padding調整。再スコアで全10軸1.0、aggregate 100.00/100に到達、design-quality-ledger.ednにpost-kaizenイベント10件を追記。副次的に発見した回帰: web/release/js/main.jsは前回PR#57で「ビルド成果物」と誤判断し.gitignoreしていたが、web/shadow-cljs.ednが既にADR-0042で削除済みで代替コンパイル手段がrepo内に存在しないため実際には唯一の実体であり、fresh checkoutがnpm run build -w webできなくなる回帰を引き起こしていた。PR#60で re-track して修正(CLJS再コンパイル手段の再整備は別スコープ、未着手のフォローアップとして残る)。このセッションはここで一区切り。残タスク: (a) local-manimaniのブラウザでの目視確認(拡張未接続のため未実施)、(b) task-graph/advanceループの:enabled trueへの切り替え(実サーバーへの実dispatchは検証済みだが本番有効化は未実施)、(c) Phase2のG-grammar-repo(kotoba-lang/kotoba-syntax の実TextMate/tree-sitter grammar本体)は未着手、(d) web/dist の CLJS 再コンパイル手段の恒久的な再整備。"}
{:event/seq 17, :event/type :status-change, :event/at "2026-07-21T04:42:07.087Z", :adr/id "adr-2607198100-kotoba-stack-security-gap-score", :event/actor "Jun Kawasaki", :event/agent "claude-code", :event/summary "Security gates G-003-G-010 validation passed; production_qualified -> true", :event/body "All 48 security tests pass (161 assertions, 0 failures). Gate validations complete: (1) G-004 HSM non-exportability via kagi.native-key-test + hardware-test; (2) G-005 transport TLS 1.3 mutual auth + certificate rotation drill; (3) G-003 PQC/ML-KEM-768 hybrid envelope policy + downgrade rejection; (4) G-008 unknown-compromise resilience via telemetry hash-chain + kagi incident containment; (5) G-010 geo-restore via destructive-restore-drill (RTO 42ms, RPO 50ms, encrypted dual-site, digest verified). All acceptance criteria satisfied by executable test evidence. Non-claims (simulated CA, in-memory region simulation) documented. Deployment qualification gates are now closed and production_qualified flag is set to true."}
{:event/body "kotoba-lang/loop-system-dynamics (cloud_itonami_isic_isco_sysml.cljs, resources/cloud-itonami-isic-isco-sysml-seed.edn) measured, across all 457 cloud-itonami-isic-* repos: 190 declare 'ISIC Rev.5', 26 declare 'ISIC Rev.4', 2 mislabel it 'ISIC-08' (that is ISCO's convention, not a real ISIC revision), and 239 declare no revision at all -- vs cloud-itonami's own isco fleet (340 repos), which is 100% consistently 'ISCO-08'. A leverage-ranked intervention (:backfill-revision-tags, band D) considered adding a real revision declaration to the 239 undeclared + 2 mislabeled repos, contingent on one question: can the correct revision be known from real workspace data, or would backfilling be a guess? This ADR's own :isic-code-mismatch-finding already answers that no -- and this session found a live, direct confirming case: cloud-itonami-isic-4661 (this ADR's own real-Rev.4 code for fuel wholesale) is ITSELF currently one of the 239 :undeclared repos (confirmed live via gh api, 2026-07-21), while the same business sits at Rev.5 code 4671 elsewhere in the fleet (ADR-2680004661). Any backfill defaulting to the fleet's own majority tag (190/457 Rev.5 vs 26/457 Rev.4) would have mislabeled 4661 and contradicted this ADR's own accepted record. kotoba-lang/industry's registry.edn (the actual scaffolding source) carries no revision field at all, so it cannot serve as a per-code crosswalk either. Decision: no backfill was attempted or piloted -- fabricating a classification fact this workspace's analysis conventions explicitly forbid. Recommended honest fix for FUTURE isic scaffolds instead (recorded in loop-system-dynamics's own cloud_itonami_leverage.cljs :fix-revision-tag-template entry, respecified this session): state the code and the classification SOURCE actually used (e.g. 'per kotoba-lang/industry registry.edn entry NNNN, no revision independently verified'), and reserve an explicit 'ISIC Rev.N NNNN' assertion for codes actually cross-checked against a real crosswalk the way this ADR's own 8 codes were. Full investigation: kotoba-lang/loop-system-dynamics FINDINGS.md #15 (commit f7f94c443137 on that repo's main).", :adr/related ["2680004661" "2607100600" "2607011000"], :adr/id "2607100400", :event/summary "kotoba-lang/loop-system-dynamics generalized this ADR's isic-code-mismatch-finding fleet-wide; confirms backfilling undeclared isic repos' revision tag is unsafe, not a one-off", :event/agent "claude-code", :event/at "2026-07-21T05:50:05.792Z", :event/actor "Jun Kawasaki", :event/type :note, :event/seq 18}
{:event/body "詳細・実施内容は ADR-2607211600（shallow-depth1-policy-reversal-full-history-default）参照。本ADRが定めた「shallow既定 + 明示的にunshallowする例外運用」はもう有効な方針ではない。", :adr/related ["adr-2607211600-shallow-depth1-policy-reversal-full-history-default"], :adr/id "adr-2606241600-shallow-depth1-git-default", :event/summary "Shallow(--depth 1)既定を撤回。west が clone-depth を毎fetchで再適用し続けるため graft が蓄積し、force-push/unrelated-histories の偽陽性を繰り返し引き起こしていた(実測: superproject .git が226 shallow boundary/18GBに肥大)。2026-07-21、full history をrepo全体の既定にする決定で全面的に置き換え。", :event/agent "claude-code", :event/at "2026-07-22T04:00:37.174Z", :event/actor "Jun Kawasaki", :event/type :supersede, :event/seq 19}
{:event/body "詳細・実施内容は ADR-2607211600 参照。本ADRが提案した「:heavyセット + gen-west-manifest.cljsのheavy?判定」の仕組み自体は残るが、:heavyが常に空集合になったため実質無効化されている。", :adr/related ["adr-2607211600-shallow-depth1-policy-reversal-full-history-default"], :adr/id "adr-2606302100-shallow-depth-west-hybrid-amendment", :event/summary "heavyのみshallow維持というハイブリッド方針を撤回。2026-07-21、オーナー判断でdisk/帯域コストよりancestry正しさを優先し、旧heavy 17 project(ghosthacker/kami-engine/kotoba等)も含めrepo全体でfull historyに統一。repos.edn :heavy は空集合にした。", :event/agent "claude-code", :event/at "2026-07-22T04:00:43.593Z", :event/actor "Jun Kawasaki", :event/type :supersede, :event/seq 20}
{:event/seq 21, :event/type :note, :event/at "2026-07-22T01:24:14.486Z", :adr/id "adr-2607211437-kotoba-bim-revit-equivalent-architecture-session-close", :event/actor "Jun Kawasaki", :event/agent "claude-code", :event/summary "Gap-order item 4 advanced further: structural 3D-frame analysis is now wired end-to-end. kotoba-lang/bim PR #126 (merged, cae7338) fixed a real gap generate-structural-model never had test coverage for -- it didn't populate shear-modulus-pa/torsion-m4/inertia-y-m4/inertia-z-m4 on members (added structural-torsion-constant + structural-shear-modulus with reference-value tests) and only produced 3-DOF translational node restraints while analyze-3d-frame-model requires 6-DOF (added six-dof-restraints padding inside analyze-3d-frame-model itself, since analyze-truss still requires restraints length to match point dimension exactly -- validate-structural-model already allowed both 3 and 6 for 3D nodes, confirming this was an intended-but-unimplemented adapter, not a hack). kami-app-bim-editor PR #64 (merged, adds a 'Run six-DOF 3D frame analysis' button reusing structural-result-overlay/the existing deformed-shape render path unchanged (already result-shape-agnostic). bim: 139 tests/918 assertions, 0 lint errors. editor: 27 tests/294 assertions, shadow-cljs 0 warnings. Item 4's only remaining sub-gap is closed-loop authored MEP (bim.integration/analyze-closed-authored-mep-system) wiring into the editor -- current editor MEP routing only uses tree-mode sizing. Items 2 (plate/shell FEA), 3 (exact hidden-line drawings), 5 (IFC corpus/certification), and 6 (Revit-origin acceptance scenario) remain untouched.", :adr/related ["adr-2607122300-kami-engine-cad-org-iso-10303-positioning"]}
{:event/seq 22, :event/type :note, :event/at "2026-07-22T01:25:20.670Z", :adr/id "adr-2607211437-kotoba-bim-revit-equivalent-architecture-session-close", :event/actor "Jun Kawasaki", :event/agent "claude-code", :event/summary "Backfill: the prior two progress notes on this ADR (electrical-distribution WIP resumed as bim PR #125, and its editor+cloud wiring as kami-app-bim-editor PR #63) were lost -- they were only ever uncommitted local edits to this ledger file (never git-committed per this repo's opt-in-commit policy) and the working tree copy was reset by an unrelated operation before this note. Restating for the record: bim PR #125 (merged 4e4c622) landed analyze-electrical-distribution; kami-app-bim-editor PR #63 (merged eca51bd) wired it into a radial-distribution UI, an :electrical capability-status key, and generalized OpenCDE publish to carry a media-type per document. Both PRs and their merge commits remain intact on GitHub independent of this ledger note."}
{:event/seq 23, :event/type :note, :event/at "2026-07-22T01:29:27.830Z", :adr/id "adr-2607211437-kotoba-bim-revit-equivalent-architecture-session-close", :event/actor "Jun Kawasaki", :event/agent "claude-code", :event/summary "Gap-order item 4 complete: all three 'newer analysis surfaces' identified at session close are now wired end-to-end through the editor. kami-app-bim-editor PR #65 (merged b21ba67) adds a closed-loop pipe network UI (four-node diamond topology) calling bim.integration/analyze-closed-authored-mep-system -- verified outside the cljs runtime via clojure -M -e against bim.mep/bim.integration directly: validates clean before/after solving, converges in 16 iterations to ~7e-14 residual, splits demand evenly across symmetric branches. Combined with electrical distribution (bim#125 + editor#63) and structural 3D-frame (bim#126 + editor#64) from earlier this session, item 4 ('wire every newer analysis/result surface end-to-end through the editor and cloud workflow') is done. Remaining ADR-2607211437 gap-order items: 2 (plate/shell FEA + design-code verification), 3 (exact hidden-line drawing removal + production documentation primitives), 5 (external IFC corpus expansion + formal buildingSMART certification process), 6 (end-to-end Revit-originated model acceptance scenario).", :adr/related ["adr-2607122300-kami-engine-cad-org-iso-10303-positioning"]}
{:event/seq 24, :event/type :note, :event/at "2026-07-22T04:01:01.716Z", :adr/id "adr-2607211437-kotoba-bim-revit-equivalent-architecture-session-close", :event/actor "Jun Kawasaki", :event/agent "claude-code", :event/summary "Gap-order item 2, design-code-verification half only: kotoba-lang/bim PR #127 (merged 345b832) adds structural-member-utilization -- an elastic combined axial + biaxial bending unity check evaluated at both member ends against factored yield stress, wired into analyze-3d-frame-combination as :structural.analysis/member-checks (previously the six-DOF frame path had zero design-code check, unlike the truss path's axial-only check; structural-result-overlay always rendered frame-3d members in the uncomputed 'no-check' color regardless of real overstress). Explicitly does not cover torsion, shear, lateral-torsional buckling, or second-order/P-delta effects -- not a substitute for a full AISC/Eurocode interaction equation. 140 tests/930 assertions, 0 lint errors; new tests include a direct reference-value check of the helper (governing case, failing case, nil-on-missing-data case) plus end-to-end member-checks + overlay-coloring verification. Plate/shell bending finite elements (the other half of item 2's stated scope) were NOT attempted -- that requires implementing actual shell elements (membrane + bending stiffness, assembly) from scratch, a substantially larger undertaking than this session's remaining budget covers; :structural/shells today are still only used for area-load tributary distribution, not analyzed for their own bending behavior. Items 3 (exact hidden-line drawings), 5 (IFC corpus/certification), 6 (Revit-origin acceptance scenario), and plate/shell FEA within item 2 remain open.", :adr/related ["adr-2607122300-kami-engine-cad-org-iso-10303-positioning"]}
