{:event/seq 29, :event/type :amend, :event/at "2026-07-22T14:17:04.206Z", :adr/id "adr-2607180400-bmc-murakumo-llm-kotobase-dual-write", :event/actor "Jun Kawasaki", :event/agent "claude-code", :event/summary "Reconciled onto current main as PR #1039 (not the original rescue PR #898); fixed a real regression found during reconciliation and relocated a transport-layer helper", :event/body "The rescued WIP (rescue/bmc-murakumo-kotobase-20260718, PR #898) deleted gftd.cli/normalize-llm-proposal (keyword-izes qwen3.6's string-typed :canvas/id / :proposal/action output, documented as a real observed model quirk) while replacing the old GFTD_LLM_URL/curl/SSE transport with gftd.murakumo, but nothing in the new resolve-advisor/compose-advisors pipeline replaced it -- LLM-mode proposals from the actual fleet-main model would have been silently dropped by the governor's keyword-only matching. Restored normalize-llm-proposal in gftd.cli and wired it into both :clj/:cljs branches of resolve-advisor via a new normalizing-advisor wrapper. Also relocated gftd.cli/strip-fences (markdown code-fence stripping) into gftd.murakumo/extract-content, matching its own docstring's stated transport-layer rationale, since it was deleted along with the old transport with nothing at the new transport layer replacing it. gftd.cli/sse-collect had no replacement and needed none -- it only reassembled the old streaming transport (ADR-2607172800), which make-complete's plain HTTP request/response supersedes outright. Verified via the bmc test runner: 31 tests / 161 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors. Landed as PR #1039 (merged 2026-07-22), which closed and superseded #898."}
{:event/seq 30, :event/type :note, :event/at "2026-07-23T08:19:06.920Z", :adr/id "adr-2607231900-russian-fleet-vessel-three-axis-filter", :event/actor "Jun Kawasaki", :event/agent "claude-code", :event/summary "Session-close checkpoint: ADR landed on main (ea8b8b49), 3-axis OR proving slice PASS (nbb), worktree/branch cleaned up; real etzhayyim integration is open follow-up.", :event/body "Merged to main via server-side gh api merges (merge sha ea8b8b497ba3843ff6d10b075ea1c719059ec39d, 2026-07-23); feat commit b7330c89 confirmed ancestor of origin/main. nbb proving slice (/tmp/russian_fleet_proof.cljs, retained for repro) ran PASS: 3-axis OR resolved IMO set {1111111, 2222222, 3333333} = flag=RU (1111111) ∪ dark-fleet (2222222, a PA-flag shadow tanker) ∪ sanctions-vessel (3333333, an LR-flag sanctioned ship) — deliberately demonstrating vessels a flag-only filter would miss. Feature branch + sparse worktree removed post-merge; integration checkout synced to origin/main (drift 0/0). OPEN follow-up NOT done this session: wire the pure 3-axis filter into the etzhayyim app-side screening function (TypeScript, app-sanctions kotoba/ side), joining vessel-registry flag + oil-shipping tanker dark-fleet flag + sanctions vessel entries by IMO. OPEN dependency: axis 2 (dark-fleet) remains :uncomputable-until-measured (ADR-2607203000) until com-etzhayyim-oil-shipping lands its tanker schema (manifest-only as of 2026-07-23)."}
